  "raw_text": "132\n\nYapi lalawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sleep through the night\n \n/ dormir toda la noche\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Rut 3:14\n):\n \nRut baha tihmia aiska Booz minakla kat yapi lalawan\n \n–\n \nRuth slept that whole night at Boaz’ feet\n \n/ Rut\ndurmió toda la noche a los pies de Boaz)\n\nYapras lalawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nnot to sleep through the night\n \n/ no dormir toda la noche\n\nNahki lalawram?\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nHow did you pass the night?\n \n/ ¿Cómo pasaste la noche?\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \nNahki buram?\n \nis a similar expression\n \n/\n \nNahki buram?\n \nes una expresión similar\n)\n\nLa\nlawra/\nLalaura\n \n–\n \nsee\n/ver:\n \nLawaia\n\nLalihkra\n \n(\ns\nee/ver:\n \nLihkaia\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nperson who likes, person who loves\n \n/ persona que le gusta, persona que\n\nama\n\nLalkamhka\n \n(a/t:\n \nLal kamhka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nforehead, skull, cranium\n \n/ frente, calavera, cráneo\n\n(Construct:\n \nLailakamhka\n;\n \nLamlakamhka\n;\n \nAi lalkamhka\n)\n\nLalma\n \n–\n \neast\n \n/ este\n\nLalma kahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto dawn, to begin to show light in the morning\n \n/ amanecer, alborear, comenzar a mostrar luz\npor la mañana\n\nLalma tani\n \n–\n \neastwards\n \n/ hacia el este\n\nLalma wina\n \n–\n \neastern, from the east, from the orient\n \n/ del este, del oriente\n\nLalmika\n \n–\n \n(the) east of\n \n/ (el) este de\n\nLalukra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nLukaia\n) (adj,n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nthinker, thoughtful, one who is thoughtful, one who thinks, one who is\nfaithful, faithful believer\n \n/ pensador, reflexivo, uno que es reflexivo, uno que piensa, uno que es fiel, fiel creyente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nupla lalukra kum wal baman marit takaia\n \n–\n \nto get married only with a believer\n \n(“only in the Lord”\n-\nnwt-\n1Kor7:39\n) /\n \ncasarse solo con un/una creyente (“solo en el Se\nñ\nor”\n-\ntnm-1Kor7:39\n))\n\nKasak lalukra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfaithful person\n \n/ persona fiel\n\nUpla lalukra apia\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nnon-\nbeliever, person who doesn’t think\n \n/ no creyente, persona que no\npiensa\n\nLalura\n \n(see/ver:\n \nLuaia\n)\n\nLama\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbreast, chest, proximity, closeness\n \n/ pecho, proximidad, cercanía\n\nLama bila\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbreast, bosom\n \n/ pecho, bosom\n\nLama dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbreastbone\n \n/ esternón\n\nLama\n \nparam\n \n–\n \nopen, open\n-\nhearted\n \n/ abierto, de corazón abierto\n\nLama pr\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nclothing to cover the chest, vest\n \n/ ropa para cubrir el pecho, chaleco\n\nLama prakaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething to cover the chest, shield\n \n/ algo para cubrir el pecho, escudo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2\n \nSam\n \n22:3\n):\n \nyang Gâdki, kaini kahbi ba walpaya, yang laima prakaika\n \n–\n \nmy God, the rock protecting me, my\nshield\n \n/ mi Dios, la roca que me protege, mi escudo)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \npr\nî\ns tara lama prakaika\n \n–\n \nbreastpiece of Israel’s high priest\n \n/\n \npectoral del sumo sacerdote\n)\n\nLama\n \nskutwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhiccup\n \n/ hipo\n\nLama skutwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hiccup\n \n/ hipar\n\nLama\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nclose, near\n \n/ cerca\n\nLamak\n \n–\n \nclose by\n \n/ cerca de\n\nLamak luaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pass close by\n \n/ pasar cerca de\n\nLamara\n \n(pos,adj)\n \n–\n \nclose\n \nto\n, near\n \nto\n \n/ cerca\n \nde\n\n(\nConstruct:\n \nL\naim\nara\n/\nLaima ra\n \n–\n \nclose/near to\n \nme / cerca de mi;\n \nLamamra\n/\nLamam ra\n \n–\n \nclose\n/near\n \nto you\n \n/ cerca de ti\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jems 4:8\n):\n \nwitin lika man nani lamamra wabia\n \n–\n \nhe will go close to you\n \n/ él se acercará a ti)\n\nKau lamara\n \n–\n \nmore close,\n \ncloser\n \n/ más cerca\n\nLamara kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be close to (physically or in friendship)\n \n/ estar cerca (físicamente o en amistad)\n\nLama uplika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nneighbor\n \n/ vecino\n\nLamaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto calm down, to become calm\n \n/ calmarse\n\nLaman\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \ncalm, still\n \n/ tranquilo, quieto\n\nLaman\n \nlâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncalm, a calm way\n, mildness\n \n/ tranquilo, de una manera tranquila,\n \napacibilidad\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \ndb\n-\nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \nuses\n \nBawaia lâka\n \nto translate\n \nmildness\n, but\n \nfy18\n \nuses\n \nLaman lâka\n \nquoting Gal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \n/\n \ndb\n-\n\nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n \nusa\n \nBawaia lâka\n \npara traducir\n \napacibilidad\n, pero\n \nfy18\n \nusa\n \nLaman lâka\n \ncitando\n \nGal\nesha\n \n5:23\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf23\n):\n \nYas man nani tilamra laman l\nȃ\nka b\nȃ\nra kabia, kan baku tnatka ra luhpiam nani ba mai aisaia lilia kabia\n \n–\n\nCause a calm way to be around you, and in that way, your children will be happy to talk to you\n \n/\n \nCrea un ambiente\n\ntranquilo de estar a su\n \nalrededor, y de esa manera,\n \ns\nus hijos estarán felices de hablar contigo)",
